invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_public returns without wiping the limbs of its base. A
  verifier's base is a signature it was sent, and the signer's is the
  candidate its check raises. A candidate that failed its check differs
  from the signature modulo one prime alone, and it and the message
  factor the modulus. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test signs under a key with one
  bit of dp changed, copies the stack below the refused call and finds
  the candidate's limbs there.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_to_bytes(out, len, acc);
    ct_wipe(x, sizeof x);
--- new
    rsa_mont64_to_bytes(out, len, acc);
